{
  "_about": [
    "Construction lines for the constructs the enchanting circle's Animate method makes (rules/constructs.py).",
    "Owner ruling 2026-11-22: 'build the magic items like wands and scrolls and constructs into the enchanting world class' - no Craft Construct feat; Enchanter levels gate them.",
    "Each row is keyed by the bestiary template the finished construct is made from (rules/bestiary.lookup), so the actor that joins is the printed stat block.",
    "`cl`, `price_gp`, `body_gp`, `spells` and `dc` are the printed Construction line (Bestiary 1-6 golem pages, the homunculus page; Ultimate Magic for animated objects, which print no line in the Bestiary). Sources: docs/research/2026-11-22-constructs.md.",
    "`spells` is a list of requirement groups: any one spell of a group meets it (the bone golem's 'animate dead or animate objects').",
    "`dc` is the printed DC; the printed DCs do not always equal 5 + CL (wood, glass, mithral), so they are data, never derived. Repairs read it too (rules/repair.py crafting_dc).",
    "`body` is what the circle takes as the body: `ingredients` from the satchel, `forged` an item the forge or the leatherworker made, or `coin_gp` for a body no bench in the app builds yet (golems), which is bought.",
    "What the code derives, never stored here: the essences (motes) are half of (price - body), 1 mote = 100 gp, the enchanting rule; the working time is the circle's 8 hours per 1,000 gp of price; the Enchanter level that may animate it is the stat block's CR rounded up (owner call, docs/research/2026-11-22-constructs.md)."
  ],
